speed.lus:8:9: hint: 'text' grows by concatenation in a loop: collect the parts in a list and call table.concat once [concat-in-loop]
speed.lus:8:16: hint: a string with interpolation writes this concatenation in one piece [use-interpolation]
speed.lus:20:9: hint: table.insert(t, 1, v) in a loop moves every element on each pass: append, then reverse the list once [insert-front-in-loop]
speed.lus:28:19: hint: this function captures nothing the loop declares: create it once before the loop [closure-in-loop]
speed.lus:37:25: hint: select(i, ...) in a loop copies the arguments on each pass: call table.pack(...) once and index it [select-in-loop]
speed.lus:43:11: hint: 'acc' never leaves this function: declare it <group> to keep its fields in locals [table-to-group]
speed.lus:55:5: hint: 'list' is a list: ipairs walks it faster and in order [pairs-over-list]
speed.lus:61:11: hint: this format holds only %s: a string with interpolation is faster [format-to-interpolation]
speed.lus:63:42: hint: concatenation converts the number itself: tostring is redundant here [redundant-tostring]
speed.lus:64:11: hint: a string with interpolation writes this concatenation in one piece [use-interpolation]
speed.lus:68:5: hint: the loop copies fields of 'r' into locals: for ... from reads them directly [use-for-from]
